gas_poor
========

Peaked dark matter in a gas cavity, in two dimensions. The distinction it measures is the one the
donor method exists for: a donor shares out a power fixed by its own mass and widens its kernel until
it finds gas to give it to, while a receiver can only heat gas that already sits where the dark matter
density is high. Moving the gas away should therefore leave the donor unaffected and starve the
receiver.

The cavity radius is the only thing that changes between runs. Gas fills a regular grid at uniform
mass everywhere outside a disc of radius R at the centre; the dark matter sits on a finer regular grid
with masses following a 3 kpc Gaussian on the same centre. Neither distribution is otherwise altered,
so the fraction of dark matter mass with no gas over it is a known function of R:

  R [kpc]        0      2      4      6      9
  fraction     0.000  0.200  0.589  0.865  0.989

Self-gravity is off and the gas is cold, so nothing moves it but the evaporation heating.

Files
-----
  make_ics.py       writes one IC per cavity radius
  gas_poor.params   GIZMO parameters; run_matrix.sh overrides the IC, OutputDir and the softening
  run_matrix.sh     builds and runs the fourteen configurations
  analyse.py        the table below and runs/gas_poor.png
  runs/             everything generated, one directory per configuration

Running
-------
From the repository root:

  python3 scripts/test_problems/outputs/gas_poor/make_ics.py
  scripts/test_problems/outputs/gas_poor/run_matrix.sh 4
  python3 scripts/test_problems/outputs/gas_poor/analyse.py

make_ics.py needs numpy and h5py; analyse.py also needs matplotlib. Neither is needed to run
the simulations themselves, only to build the initial conditions and read the results.

MFM throughout. Fourteen configurations take about 25 minutes on four tasks.

The kernel ceiling
------------------
A donor may widen its kernel to 100 times All.ForceSoftening, and ForceSoftening is 2.8 times the
Plummer-equivalent softening in the parameter file for the cubic spline. SofteningHalo = 0.078 kpc
therefore lets a donor search 21.8 kpc, wider than the half-width of the box, so no cavity that fits
in the box can starve it. The two shortreach runs set SofteningHalo = 0.020 kpc instead, putting the
ceiling at 5.6 kpc, which is inside the 9 kpc cavity. With self-gravity off the softening does nothing
else here, so it is a clean knob on the ceiling alone.

Results
-------
Instantaneous power coupled as a fraction of the analytic total, at the start and end of the run; the
same fraction integrated over the run; and for donor runs the lowest per-step coupled fraction the
budget report saw, with the number of donors that had no gas in reach at that step.

  config                 power t=0  power t=end   whole-run  worst-coupled
  r0_pbhef1               0.999264     0.998566    0.998607  -
  r2_pbhef1               0.807508     0.993366    0.914861  -
  r4_pbhef1               0.422202     0.945046    0.589454  -
  r6_pbhef1               0.140623     0.271028    0.173310  -
  r9_pbhef1               0.011713     0.013218    0.012131  -
  r0_pbhef2               0.999996     0.999998    1.000000  1.000000 (0 starved)
  r2_pbhef2               0.999996     0.999998    1.000000  1.000000 (0 starved)
  r4_pbhef2               0.999996     0.999998    1.000017  1.000000 (0 starved)
  r6_pbhef2               0.999995     0.999998    1.000047  1.000000 (0 starved)
  r9_pbhef2               0.999995     0.999998    0.999999  1.000000 (0 starved)
  r9_pbhef2_iso           0.999996     0.999998    0.999999  1.000000 (0 starved)
  r9_pbhef1_shortreach    0.011713     0.013218    0.012131  -
  r9_pbhef2_shortreach    0.524114     0.999997    0.772050  0.524116 (6009 starved)

The receiver couples the fraction of dark matter that has gas over it, and nothing more. Against the
table at the top of this file: 0.808 where 0.800 of the mass is covered, 0.422 against 0.411, 0.141
against 0.135, 0.0117 against 0.0111. It runs a little above each because its own kernel is 16 dark
matter neighbours wide, so mass just inside the rim is still seen by the gas cells just outside it.
The donor couples 1.000 at every radius, under both weightings.

The receiver recovers at small radii and not at large ones: 0.81 to 0.99 at 2 kpc, 0.42 to 0.95 at
4 kpc, but only 0.14 to 0.27 at 6 kpc and 0.012 to 0.013 at 9 kpc. It suppresses its own heating
exactly where the gas is missing, so there is nothing to drive gas back and the suppression holds.

The donor's coupled fraction also returns to 1.000 when the ceiling is short enough to starve it, and
that recovery is worth looking at closely rather than taking at face value. The heated rim expands
outwards, as it must: mean radial velocity in the 8 to 11 kpc shell of the shortreach run runs +0.016,
+0.272 and +0.893 km/s over the four snapshots. What reaches the middle is a thin tongue of gas
expanding into the vacuum on the inward-facing side, and by the end of the run 32 cells out of 55108
sit inside 5 kpc, carrying 0.048 of 82.66 in mass. Those 32 cells receive 69.3 per cent of the total
evaporation power, at a specific heating rate four orders of magnitude above the median and an internal
energy five orders above it. Nothing goes unstable here, and the run ends in a single timebin, but the
budget is balanced by concentrating almost all of the energy onto six hundredths of a per cent of the
gas mass. Whether that is preferable to dropping it is a physics question, not a bookkeeping one.

So the report has to be read as a minimum over the run rather than a final value, and for two reasons
rather than one. It hides the starved phase, and the state it reports as healthy is the concentrated
one. The starved phase itself is detected cleanly: 0.524116 with the donor count short by exactly the
6009 that had no gas in reach, so no code change is needed to see the condition arise.
